ware -> /, /about-us, /services", "Emphasizes ability to make virtually any metal component -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We do complete layout and fabrication in our shop with cutting, welding and forming equipment.", "founded_year": "1928", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olson-sheet-metal-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Olsun Electrics Corporation operates from Richmond, Illinois, where it was established in 1950 to serve the electronics industry in the greater Chicago area. The company began in a downtown Richmond building that housed a dentist office in front and a hand-crafted dry-type transformer operation in the back. Gus Asta, one of the original partners, purchased the business in 1965 and expanded the product scope to power and distribution transformers and reactors. The company remains family-run and, on October 28, 2019, earned Women''s Business Enterprise (WBE) certification through WBENC, confirming it is at least 51% owned, operated, and controlled by women.

The company designs and manufactures dry-type transformers ranging from 5 kVA through 5,000 kVA in voltage classes up to 34.5 kV, offering 15 distinct product types that include general-purpose, substation, encapsulated, cast-coil, pad-mounted, marine-duty, harmonic-mitigating, and triplex designs. In-house capabilities span design engineering, coil winding (barrel, disc, and block), vacuum-pressure impregnation, core cutting and stacking, enclosure fabrication — now aided by a Bystronic 4 kW fiber laser with automated material handling — powder coating, encapsulation, bus-bar fabrication, and final assembly and testing to NEMA ST-20 and ANSI C57.12.01/91 standards.

Olsun serves a broad range of sectors: universities and student housing, hospitals and healthcare, oil and gas (including portable power for land rigs), petrochemical plants, renewable natural gas and battery energy storage, electric-vehicle charging infrastructure, commercial HVAC OEMs, architectural glass fabrication, ship-to-shore crane systems, and marine/offshore installations (ABS/DNV compliant). The company also supports brand-label and OEM accounts, a segment it has served continuously since the 1960s.

Olsun emphasizes design flexibility and craftsmanship as its differentiators: the ability to produce one-of-a-kind custom transformers when off-the-shelf units will not fit, backed by decades-experienced coil winders and engineers. The firm was founded to meet exacting OEM requirements and continues to position itself as a partner for intricate, standards-compliant solutions rather than a commodity supplier.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed / cUL Listed','NEMA ST-20','ANSI C57.12.01','ANSI C57.12.91','IEEE standards','IEC standards','WBENC Women''s Business Enterprise (WBE) Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design engineering for custom transformers", "Coil winding (barrel, disc, block) with wire and foil", "Vacuum pressure impregnation (VPI) epoxy varnish system", "Miter and butt-lap core cutting and stacking", "Core and coil assembly", "Enclosure fabrication (shear, punch, form, laser cutting)", "Base and clamp fabrication (structural steel welding)", "Powder coat paint system (multi-stage wash, electrostatically applied, oven cured)", "Encapsulation (polyester resin and silica sand)", "Bus bar fabrication (aluminum or copper)", "Final assembly with interrupter switches, rotary tap switches", "Retrofit and replacement transformer manufacturing", "EV charging station transformer solutions (LV and MV substations)", "Testing to NEMA ST-20, ANSI C57.12.01, C57.12.91"], "industries": ["Higher education (universities, student housing)", "Healthcare (hospitals)", "Oil and gas (land drilling, portable power)", "Petrochemical", "Renewable energy (battery storage, natural gas generation)", "Electric vehicle charging infrastructure", "Commercial HVAC OEM", "Architectural glass fabrication", "Marine and offshore (ship-to-shore cranes, ABS/DNV)", "Industrial automation", "Utility and power distribution"], "materials": ["Copper wire and foil", "Aluminum wire and foil", "Electrical steel (core laminations)", "Epoxy varnish", "Polyester resin", "Silica sand", "Steel channel, angle, and bar stock", "Powder coat paint"], "equipment": ["Bystronic 4 kW Fiber Laser Cutting Machine with Material Loading and Unloading Automation", "Miter and butt-lap core cutters", "Stacking table fixtures", "Vacuum pressure chamber for VPI", "Dip tank for epoxy varnish coating", "Powder coat wash/pretreat system and oven", "Overhead cranes (2\u201320 ton capacity, six total)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom design and manufacturing under one roof", "One-off manufacturing capability for intricate designs", "In-house enclosure fabrication with fiber laser cutting automation", "Retrofit and replacement transformer expertise with dedicated forms", "WBENC-certified Women''s Business Enterprise (2019)", "Family-run with decades-experienced craftspeople"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1950 in Richmond, Illinois -> /about-us", "Gus Asta purchased company in 1965 -> /about-us", "Family-run, WBENC WBE certified Oct 28 2019 -> /about-us", "86,000 sq ft facility, 35-ft walls, six cranes 2-20 ton -> /about-us", "Transformers 5 kVA\u20135,000 kVA through 34.5 kV, 15 product types -> /about-us", "In-house design, winding, VPI, core cutting, enclosure fab, powder coat, encapsulation, bus bar, final assembly -> /capabilities", "Bystronic 4 kW fiber laser with automation for enclosure fabrication -> /", "Industries: universities, hospitals, oil/gas, petrochemical, renewable, EV charging, HVAC, marine, architectural glass -> / (recent projects)", "UL/cUL marks, NEMA, ANSI, IEEE, IEC, ABS, DNV compliance -> /about-us", "Brand-label/OEM accounts since 1960s -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Olsun Electrics is a leading dry type transformer manufacturing company that has been providing solutions in the most challenging environments and applications for over seven decades.", "founded_year": "1950", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [