UPDATE companies SET description='Olympic Controls Corporation was founded in 1968 and operates from a 61,000-square-foot facility in Bartlett, Illinois, with an additional 25,000-square-foot plant in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.

The company manufactures a range of electrical components including current and potential transformers, switchgear components, custom transformers, T-Bar switches, fuel pumps, relays, and custom-wound coils.

Its customer base spans aerospace and avionics, military and defense, commercial power distribution, data centers, and solar farms. Named clients include BAE Systems, Eaton, General Dynamics, Lockheed Martin, Raytheon Technologies, Siemens, the U.S. Air Force, U.S. Navy, and the Department of Defense.

Olympic Controls differentiates itself through 100 percent U.S. production, a no-minimum-order policy, typical lead times of four to six weeks after receipt of order, and a one-year warranty on all products. The company cites its ISO 9001 certification and a family-employee-client ethos as the foundation of its integrity.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom-wound coils", "Custom transformer engineering", "Precision relay manufacturing", "Switchgear component manufacturing (CTs, PTs)", "T-Bar switch manufacturing", "Fuel pump assembly", "CAD/CAM design services", "Electrical component assembly"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Avionics", "Military", "Defense", "Commercial power distribution", "Data centers", "Solar farms", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Zinc", "Plated hardware"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Typical lead times 4\u20136 weeks ARO depending on product specifications", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order quantity", "100% U.S. domestic production", "Typical lead times 4\u20136 weeks ARO", "Over 50 years of manufacturing experience", "ISO 9001 certified quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1968 -> db, homepage", "120 employees -> db, homepage", "61,000 sq ft facility in Bartlett, Illinois -> homepage", "25,000 sq ft facility in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania -> homepage", "Clients: BAE Systems, Eaton, General Dynamics, Lockheed Martin, Raytheon Technologies, Siemens, U.S. Air Force, U.S. Navy, Department of Defense -> homepage", "ISO 9001 certified -> db, homepage", "No minimum order quantity -> homepage", "Lead times typically 4\u20136 weeks ARO -> homepage", "Products: CTs, PTs, switchgear components, custom transformers, T-Bar switches, fuel pumps, relays, custom-wound coils -> homepage", "Industries: aerospace, avionics, military, defense, commercial power distribution, data centers, solar farms, industrial -> homepage, industries_served", "Family-oriented culture mentioned -> homepage", "100% U.S. domestic production -> homepage", "1-year warranty -> homepage", "CAD/CAM services offered -> homepage", "Zinc pump body with plated hardware -> products list"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "OEM manufacturer of electrical components \u2014 from switchgear and transformers to relays, coils, and fuel pumps.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "120", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olympic-controls-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Olympus Manufacturing is based in Orem, Utah. The company was founded by brothers Jake and Matt Crowder, who started the business out of a shared passion for creation and a desire to help other brands bring their ideas to life. While a specific founding year is not publicly disclosed, the founders describe the origin as a love for making things that evolved into a mission to empower entrepreneurs and established companies alike.

The company provides custom manufacturing and private label services focused on dietary supplements and nutraceutical products. Its custom manufacturing process covers formula development, ingredient selection, and packaging design tailored to each client''s specifications. For brands seeking faster market entry, Olympus offers a line of ready-made stock formulations that can be packaged and labeled under the client''s brand.

Its customer base ranges from aspiring entrepreneurs launching their first product to established businesses expanding their supplement lines. The company cites work with both startups and mature brands as evidence of its flexible approach.

The founders state that the business was built to remove barriers for brand owners, offering flexible, high-quality solutions with low minimums and hands-on guidance. They position their differentiators as personalized service, formulation expertise, and a willingness to work with companies at any stage of growth.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Manufacturing", "Private Label Products", "Customized Product Formulation", "Packaging and Labeling Customization", "Product Development", "Formulation"], "industries": ["Dietary Supplements", "Nutraceuticals", "Health and Wellness"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Personalized support throughout product development", "Custom formulation tailored to brand specifications", "Ready-made private label stock products", "Flexible manufacturing for startups and established brands"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Jake and Matt Crowder -> /", "Headquartered in Orem, Utah -> db", "Offers custom manufacturing and private label services -> /", "Provides low minimum order quantities -> /", "Serves aspiring entrepreneurs and established businesses -> /", "Focus on supplement and nutraceutical products -> /", "Emphasizes personalized support and flexible solutions -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom manufacturing and private label services", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='olympus-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Omni Defense Tech was founded on November 20, 1998 in Colchester, Vermont by Mark Harvie, an electromechanical engineer with a passion for aviation and technology. The company began as a small engineering firm focused on solving life-support challenges for aviators.

Today the company designs, develops, and manufactures in-flight bladder relief systems under the SKYDRATE brand, along with certified through-suit connectors that maintain environmental seals for immersion suits and chemical-biological-radiological-nuclear (CBRN) protective gear. Its product line includes male and female relief devices and tactical flotation systems for parachutists. Omni Defense holds eleven U.S. patents and collaborates with NASA on waste-management systems for astronauts, with products deployed worldwide.

The primary customers are military aviators, including U.S. Air Force and U.S. Navy pilots and partner-nation forces, as well as chem-bio protection personnel, search-and-rescue teams, and medical professionals. The SKYDRATE system has passed rigorous flight-safety testing by the USAF and USN and is used on platforms such as the F-15E. NASA also relies on the company''s technology for spaceflight waste management.

The business was started to address tactical dehydration, which can reduce pilot performance by 57 percent, and to provide a relief method that does not require aircrew to unstrap from safety restraints. The company emphasizes that its connectors are certified to maintain suit integrity in extreme environments, and that its hands-free, leak-proof design sets a new standard for in-flight bladder relief.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design and development of life-support systems", "Manufacturing of in-flight bladder relief systems (SKYDRATE)", "Through-suit connector fabrication for immersion and CBRN suits", "Tactical flotation device production", "Flight safety testing and certification", "NASA space waste-management system development"], "industries": ["Military aviation", "Chemical-biological protection", "Search and rescue", "Medical equipment", "Space exploration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["SKYDRATE system passes U.S. Air Force and U.S. Navy flight-safety standards", "Through-suit connector maintains environmental seal on immersion suits and CBRN gear", "Relief system operates without requiring aircrew to unstrap from safety restraints", "Eleven U.S. patents and global deployment", "NASA collaboration for astronaut waste-management systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded November 20, 1998 by Mark Harvie -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Colchester, Vermont -> db", "Designs, develops, manufactures in-flight bladder relief systems -> /", "SKYDRATE system passes USAF/USN flight safety standards -> /", "Through-suit connector maintains environmental seal for immersion suits and CBRN gear -> /", "Products for military, chem-bio, search and rescue, medical -> /", "Collaboration with NASA for space waste management -> /about-us", "Eleven US patents -> /about-us", "Tactical flotation devices -> /about-us", "Tactical dehydration reduces pilot performance by 57% -> /", "System does not require unstrapping from safety restraints -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Omni Defense Technologies designs, develops, and manufactures best-in-class products that support military Aviators on all aircrew ensembles.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='omni-defense-tech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='One Semiconductor was founded in 2011 in Austin, Texas. The company began as a specialist in semiconductor equipment lifecycle solutions, focusing on refurbishment, precision component manufacturing, and system upgrades for advanced production equipment.

The company provides refurbishment, upgrades, thermal management, and lifecycle solutions for 200 mm and 300 mm semiconductor manufacturing equipment. Its service portfolio includes sub-assembly repair and parts supply, technology upgrades and retrofits such as controller retrofits and system enhancements, on-site maintenance and field service covering preventive and corrective maintenance, and complete equipment refurbishment and overhaul for etch and deposition tools. It also manufactures precision components for semiconductor equipment.

One Semiconductor serves wafer fabrication facilities, test and inspection platforms, and assembly operations across the global semiconductor market. Its customers include OEMs and suppliers in North America, Asia, and Latin America who require cost-effective alternatives to equipment replacement.

The company emphasizes engineering-driven solutions with transparent execution, proven experience in semiconductor equipment services, global reach with fast response times, and flexible service models. Its culture is rooted in engineering excellence, technical expertise, and long-term industry partnerships, prioritizing transparency and collaboration with customers, OEMs, and suppliers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor equipment refurbishment", "Equipment overhaul", "Technology upgrades and retrofits", "Controller retrofits", "System enhancements", "On-site maintenance and field service", "Preventive maintenance", "Corrective maintenance", "Sub-assembly repair", "Parts supply", "Precision component manufacturing", "Etch tool refurbishment", "Deposition tool refurbishment", "Thermal management solutions", "Equipment conversion"], "industries": ["Semiconductor manufacturing", "Wafer fabrication", "Test and inspection", "Assembly operations"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proven experience in semiconductor equipment services", "Global service capabilities and fast response times", "Cost-effective alternatives to equipment replacement", "Engineering-driven solutions with transparent execution"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Austin, Texas -> db", "Services: refurbishment, upgrades, thermal management, lifecycle solutions for 200mm/300mm equipment -> /", "Sub-assembly repair & parts supply -> /", "Technology upgrades & retrofits (controller retrofits, system enhancements) -> /", "On-site maintenance & field service (preventive, corrective) -> /", "Equipment refurbishment & overhaul for etch and deposition tools -> /", "Precision component manufacturing -> /about-us", "Industries: wafer fabrication facilities, test and inspection platforms, assembly operations -> /about-us", "Global presence in North America, Asia, Latin America -> /about-us", "Differentiators: proven experience, global capabilities, cost-effective alternatives, engineering-driven solutions -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "specializes in semiconductor equipment lifecycle solutions, including refurbishment, precision component manufacturing, and system upgrades", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='one-semiconductor' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ontogen Medtech operates from Lisle, Illinois, and began in 2021 with a mission to give medical device innovators a strategy-focused, capital-efficient path from concept to commercialization.

The firm provides end-to-end product development, including design, prototyping, engineering, and comprehensive in-house testing and validation, alongside ISO 13485 certified contract manufacturing and regulatory support. Its team integrates senior talent directly into client programs to execute prototyping, engineering, and testing rather than only advising. The company reports that its clients have collectively secured more than $16.6 million in grant funding, obtained over 132 patents, won $2.2 million in pitch competitions, and shipped thousands of devices nationwide.

Ontogen serves medical device startups and innovators developing electro-mechanical, reusable, surgical, single-use, and diagnostic devices. Named clients include Flow Medical, Stiehl Tech, Innoblative, and Hubly Surgical, which have relied on the company for everything from SBIR grant support and verification testing to 510(k) clearance and commercial launch.

The company says its differentiation lies in acting as a single, end-to-end partner that eliminates handoff gaps, embedding senior staff in the trenches to deliver tangible deliverables—clear requirements, disciplined design history files, risk rigor, and verification plans—rather than racking up meetings. It describes itself as the most transparent partner in medtech, focusing on evidence over activity.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product development", "Design and prototyping", "Engineering", "Testing and validation", "In-house testing", "Contract manufacturing", "ISO 13485 certified production", "Regulatory support and compliance", "Design controls (DHF)", "Risk management", "Verification planning", "SBIR grant support", "Clinical validation support", "510(k) clearance support"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Electro-mechanical devices", "Reusable devices", "Surgical devices", "Single-use devices", "Diagnostic devices", "Medical device startups", "Medical device innovators"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end partner from regulatory strategy through ISO 13485 manufacturing", "Senior talent directly executes prototyping, engineering, and testing", "Focus on deliverables that de-risk programs (requirements, DHF, risk, verification)", "Transparent, evidence-based approach rather than activity-based billing"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2021 -> /about", "Headquarters in Lisle, Illinois -> db", "ISO 13485 certified -> db, /", "Services: product development, contract manufacturing, regulatory support -> /", "Clients: Flow Medical, Stiehl Tech, Innoblative, Hubly Surgical -> /", "Statistics: $16.6M+ grants, 132+ patents, $2.2M+ prizes, 1000''s devices shipped -> /", "Differentiators: end-to-end, hands-on, evidence-based -> /about", "Device types: electro-mechanical, reusable, surgical, single-use, diagnostic -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Contract Manufacturing\nISO 13485 Certified Production", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/ontogenmedtech/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ontogen-medtech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Onyx Electronics Inc. was founded in 1990 in Olathe, Kansas. The company began as a manufacturer of precision pressure instrumentation for industrial applications and has remained U.S.-based throughout its history.

Today, Onyx produces pressure instruments and integrates them with process control panels, telemetry systems, SCADA software, and data logging equipment. The company operates from a facility on West Highway 56 in Olathe, serving customers across the United States with a focus on combining sensing hardware with software and communication platforms.

The company’s products are used in industrial settings that require precise pressure measurement and control.

Onyx emphasizes its domestic manufacturing and the ability to combine pressure sensing with broader control and data acquisition platforms, offering a single-source solution for pressure instrumentation and system integration.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision pressure instrument manufacturing", "Process control panel integration", "Telemetry system integration", "SCADA software integration", "Data logging equipment integration", "System integration services"], "industries": ["Industrial pressure instrumentation", "Process automation", "Industrial manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-based manufacturing of precision pressure instruments since 1990", "Integration of pressure instruments with process control panels", "Telemetry system and SCADA software integration", "Data logging equipment integration", "Single-source instrumentation and control solutions"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 -> db", "Headquarters in Olathe, KS -> page /", "Manufactures precision pressure instrumentation -> description", "Integrates pressure instruments with process control panels, telemetry systems, SCADA software, and data logging equipment -> description", "Address: 1351 W Hwy 56 Suite E, Olathe, KS 66061 -> page /", "Contact phone, fax, and email -> page /", "Website: http://www.onyxelectronicsinc.com/page11.php -> db", "Industries served: Manufacturing Precision Pressure Instruments for Industry -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Onyx Electronics has been manufacturing precision pressure instrumentation since 1990 in the USA.", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='onyx-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ozark Biomedical operates from Beebe, Arkansas, where it was founded in 2007.

The company supplies replacement parts and performs repairs for a wide range of centrifuge models from manufacturers including Beckman, Thermo Fisher, Eppendorf, Hettich, and others. Its core manufacturing activity is the remanufacture of motors, latches, and circuit boards to meet or exceed original OEM specifications. Ozark Biomedical also offers products on an exchange basis, requiring return of a repairable core, and provides recertified and remanufactured centrifuges with limited parts warranties.

A noted client is Novum Pharmaceutical Research Services.

