UPDATE companies SET description='Paradigm Foodworks Inc operates from Lake Oswego, Oregon, where it has been producing small-batch artisanal foods since 1981.

These include charcuterie condiments, dessert sauces, fruit and berry spreads, barbecue and grill sauces, mustards and horseradish, pizza and pasta sauces, salad dressings, salsa and enchilada sauces, as well as Indian-inspired Masala Maza and Asian fusion Heaven & Earth lines. Specific items such as Apple Jalapeño Jelly, Apricot Cognac Conserve, and Arrabbiata Sauce illustrate the flavor breadth. Production is described as small batch, though facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not disclosed.

Paradigm Foodworks sells directly to consumers through its e-commerce website, shipping to addresses within the contiguous 48 United States with free shipping on orders over $75.

The company emphasizes its long-standing commitment to small-batch craftsmanship, a practice maintained since its 1981 founding. Its woman-owned status further distinguishes it in the specialty food sector.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman-owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Small batch food production", "Sauce and condiment manufacturing", "Fruit preserve and jelly making", "Artisanal flavor formulation", "Bottling and packaging"], "industries": ["Specialty foods", "Condiments and sauces", "Fruit preserves and spreads", "Gourmet food products", "Retail food manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Small batch production since 1981", "Woman-owned business", "Direct-to-consumer shipping across the contiguous U.S.", "Free shipping on orders over $75", "Diverse artisanal product lines spanning global flavor profiles"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 -> db", "Headquarters Lake Oswego, Oregon -> db", "Woman-owned certification -> db", "Small Batch Crafted Since 1981 -> page /", "Product lines: charcuterie condiments, dessert sauces, fruit & berry spreads, BBQ & grill sauces, mustards & horseradish, pizza & pasta sauces, salad dressings, salsa & enchilada sauces, Masala Maza Indian sauces, Heaven & Earth Asian fusion sauces -> page /", "Specific products: Apple Jalape\u00f1o Jelly, Apricot Cognac Conserve, Arrabbiata Sauce -> page /", "Shipping to US addresses only, free shipping at $75 for contiguous 48 states -> page /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Small Batch Crafted Since 1981", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paradigm-foodworks-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The studio was founded in 2015 by Jon Anglesey, who brought 35 years of hands-on experience designing, building, and installing custom cabinetry. Anglesey established the company to elevate custom cabinetry from a standard trade into an architectural discipline, applying field-tested knowledge to every design and layout that leaves the studio.

The shop produces architectural-grade custom cabinetry and bespoke millwork, specializing in high-precision frameless construction with interlocking blind-dado joinery glued and screwed at every joint. Cabinet boxes use CARB-compliant, formaldehyde-free thermally fused laminate platforms; drawers feature 3/4-inch sidewalls, 1/2-inch bottoms, and Italian Salice rack-and-pinion full-extension slides rated 33 to 50 pounds above competing hardware. Finishes are Italian waterborne urethanes with a proprietary cross-linker, delivering zero-VOC, zero-HAPP surface protection. Two product lines serve different project scopes: the Custom Shop Series offers unrestricted design, shadow-line detailing, and integrated LED case lighting, while the ECO Line standardizes flat-slab profiles with pre-engineered subcrowns to cut field installation time by two-thirds and reduce cost by 25 to 35 percent.

Paragon serves architects, designers, builders, and homeowners across nine Northern Utah counties — Box Elder, Cache, Weber, Davis, Morgan, Salt Lake, Summit, Utah, and Wasatch — covering the entire Wasatch Front corridor. Projects span luxury kitchens, bathroom vanities, integrated library and office systems, entertainment hubs, laundry rooms, and tailored closets. The team manages each commission from initial architectural layout through zero-tolerance final installation.

The company''s stated differentiation rests on four pillars: total transparency in materials, pricing, and methods; technical innovation through advanced design software and disciplined fabrication; environmental stewardship via sustainably sourced, low-emission materials; and architectural respect for the client''s space, investment, and the timber resources used. Anglesey''s direct involvement in every design ensures that details derived from decades of field installation — reveal alignment, drawer load capacity, joinery that accommodates structural settlement — are baked into the plans before fabrication begins.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Frameless cabinet construction", "Blind-dado joinery", "Custom kitchen cabinetry", "Bathroom vanity frameworks", "Integrated millwork & library systems", "Architectural entertainment centers", "Laundry room cabinetry", "Closet systems & built-ins", "Custom Shop Series (bespoke)", "ECO Line (standardized sustainable)", "Zero-VOC waterborne urethane finishing", "CARB-compliant material sourcing", "Design consultation & engineering submittals", "White-glove installation", "Project management from layout to install"], "industries": ["Luxury residential construction", "Architectural millwork", "Kitchen & bath design", "Interior design", "Custom furniture", "Home remodeling"], "materials": ["CARB-compliant non-formaldehyde TFL (thermally fused laminate)", "Italian waterborne urethane finishes", "Solid wood (responsibly harvested)", "Melamine (Classic White)", "Birch (Architectural)", "Walnut (Dark Textured)", "Woven fabric (Luxe)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Interlocking blind-dado box construction glued and screwed at every joint", "Italian Salice rack-and-pinion drawer slides with 33\u201350 lb higher load rating than major competitors", "Zero-VOC Italian waterborne urethane finishes with proprietary cross-linker", "ECO Line reduces on-site installation time by two-thirds and cabinetry cost by 25\u201335%", "Founder Jon Anglesey personally oversees every design and layout, drawing on 35 years of field experience"], "facts_used": ["Location: Pleasant View, Utah -> /", "Founded 2015 by Jon Anglesey -> /about", "35 years bench experience -> /about", "Serves 9 Northern Utah counties -> /", "Frameless construction with blind-dado joinery -> /", "CARB-compliant, formaldehyde-free TFL platforms -> /", "3/4\" drawer sidewalls, 1/2\" bottoms -> /", "Italian Salice rack-and-pinion slides, 33-50 lb higher rating -> /", "Zero-VOC Italian waterborne urethane finishes -> /", "Custom Shop Series vs ECO Line differences -> /", "ECO Line cuts install time 2/3, cost 25-35% -> /, /services", "Custom Shop offers unrestricted design, shadow-line, LED lighting -> /, /services", "Services: kitchens, bathrooms, libraries, entertainment, laundry, closets -> /, /services", "Installation across Wasatch Front corridor -> /", "Four pillars: transparency, innovation, stewardship, respect -> /about", "Sustainably sourced, low-emission materials -> /about", "Founder involvement in every design -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "engineer architectural cabinetry from a single shop floor in Pleasant View", "founded_year": "2015", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paragon-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Parts Unlimited Interiors, Inc. is based in La Grange, Kentucky, operating from a 120,000-square-foot facility in the Oldham County Business Park. The business traces its origins to 1974 when Rollo Fox and his wife Colleen, inspired by Colleen''s father H.V. Morris, attended a Corvair convention in Chicago and sold parts from their car trunk. What began as a new-old-stock parts venture soon evolved into manufacturing Corvair interior components, then expanded to other GM models. The company moved from the Morris family basement to the Jefferson Trade Center in December 1984, then to a 51,400-square-foot plant in Louisville, before settling in its current location. Since October 2023, PUI has been a subsidiary of Classic Industries, following an earlier acquisition by Restoration Parts Unlimited in 2013.

PUI manufactures interior soft-trim and hard-goods for classic American vehicles, including seat upholstery, door panels, headliners, window felts, and insulation products. Production relies on a mix of computer-controlled machinery and hands-on oversight by more than 80 artisans, many with decades of tenure. The facility houses sophisticated equipment for cutting, sewing, and assembling a wide range of materials. Approximately 97–98% of PUI''s products are made in the United States, with the remainder sourced overseas. The company maintains a large inventory to support same-day and next-day shipping on stocked items.

The company serves the automotive aftermarket and classic-car restoration markets, supplying wholesale dealers and individual restorers. Its product lines cover GM brands (Chevrolet Impala, Pontiac, Buick), Ford, and Mopar vehicles. PUI sells through over 100 dealers across the U.S. and internationally, and offers exclusive wholesale pricing to registered partners.

The Foxes originally started the business to address the finite supply of NOS Corvair parts, shifting to reproduction to keep the company viable. Today, PUI emphasizes domestic manufacturing, a deep catalog of pattern-specific parts, and reduced lead times—raw-material sourcing now takes two to three weeks, and dealer delivery is under one month—following supply-chain improvements after the Classic Industries acquisition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Interior soft trim manufacturing", "Seat upholstery production", "Door panel manufacturing", "Headliner production", "Window felt manufacturing", "Insulation manufacturing", "Computer-controlled machining", "Artisan hand-finishing"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Classic car restoration", "Automotive interior restoration"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Less than one month for dealer delivery; same-day/next-day shipping for stocked parts", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["97\u201398% of products manufactured in the USA", "Same-day and next-day shipping on stocked parts", "Over 80 artisans with decades of experience", "Raw material lead time reduced to 2\u20133 weeks", "Dealer delivery lead time under one month"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1974 by Rollo and Colleen Fox -> /about-us", "Headquarters in La Grange, KY, 120,000 sq ft facility -> /about-us", "Over 100 employees -> db", "97-98% US manufactured -> /about-us", "Acquired by Restoration Parts Unlimited 2013, then Classic Industries 2023 -> /about-us", "Manufactures seat upholstery, door panels, headliners, window felts, insulation -> /about-us", "Serves GM, Ford, Mopar classic vehicles -> /", "Same-day/next-day shipping on stocked parts -> /", "Wholesale pricing for dealers -> /", "Lead times reduced to under one month for dealers -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Parts Unlimited Interiors manufactures the finest interior soft trim products for the classic Impala models", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='parts-unlimited-interiors-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pascetti Steel Design, Inc. operates from Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a family-owned custom steel fabricator. The company was founded by Damian Pascetti, who spent his career working with steel beginning in his father’s structural steel business before opening his own shop. The business remains family-owned and managed, with Pascetti overseeing projects directly.

The shop delivers complete turnkey solutions for commercial and residential steel projects, handling design, shop drawings, fabrication, delivery, and installation. Core offerings include steel stair and railing systems, custom balconies, canopies, architectural features, large-scale light fixtures, perforated metal panels, shade structures, gates, and signage. The team also takes on historic restoration work and has fabricated custom gym equipment such as the patent-pending Phat Rack™ heavy-bag system. Work is designed in CAD and prefabricated for field installation.

Clients range from architects, designers, and homeowners to public institutions and commercial contractors. Notable projects include railing restorations at historic landmarks in Albuquerque, Durango, Colorado, and Dayton, Ohio; a church frame for original Tiffany stained glass; a bell display at the University of New Mexico; and the Penguin Chill exhibit at the ABQ BioPark. The company also serves local gyms and residential customers seeking custom metalwork.

Pascetti Steel emphasizes personalized service, noting that its small, family-owned structure allows management to oversee every project. The firm states it welcomes complex, one-of-a-kind projects that other fabricators may avoid, aiming to deliver durable, high-quality steelwork built to exceed expectations. Its mission centers on fostering strong relationships and being a partner in metal fabrication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom steel fabrication", "Steel stair and railing packages", "Custom balcony fabrication", "Steel canopy fabrication", "Large commercial light fixture fabrication", "Perforated metal panel fabrication", "Shade structure fabrication", "Gate fabrication", "Signage fabrication", "Historic restoration", "Custom gym equipment fabrication", "Design and shop drawing preparation", "CAD design", "Prefabrication", "Delivery and installation"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Historic preservation", "Public art and exhibits", "Fitness and recreation", "Municipal and institutional", "Architectural metalwork"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Perforated metal"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey service from design and shop drawings through fabrication, delivery, and installation", "Willingness to take on complex, one-of-a-kind projects other fabricators avoid", "Family-owned operation with management oversight on every project", "Experience with historic restoration projects meeting strict landmark requirements", "Custom-engineered gym equipment systems (Phat Rack\u2122 patent pending)"], "facts_used": ["Location: Albuquerque, New Mexico -> /", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Owner: Damian Pascetti -> /about-us", "Services: custom steel fabrication, stairs, railings, balconies, canopies, light fixtures -> /", "Turnkey solutions from design to installation -> /", "Historic restoration projects in Albuquerque, Durango, Dayt