UPDATE companies SET description='Port Clinton Manufacturing Co. has operated from Port Clinton, Ohio, since its founding in 1929. The company remains a closely held family corporation, locally owned and operated across nearly a century of continuous service.

A broaching department runs 12 machines with a 54-inch stroke and 15-ton capacity, while grinding operations cover ID, OD, centerless, double-disk, and Blanchard processes. Secondary machining includes thread rolling, knurling, drilling, tapping, cross drilling, deep-hole drilling, honing, milling, tumbling, bead blasting, and a range of cutoff and forming operations. Heat treating and coating are managed through a qualified external network. The company also performs ultrasonic cleaning and Millipore particle-count testing. Precision assemblies — joined by brazing or mechanical fits — are produced in-house, either as finished units or as in-process components brought to final tolerance after assembly.

Primary markets include railroad, oil and gas, mining, emergency power generation, agricultural and construction equipment, mine safety devices, heavy-truck transmissions, and brake systems. As a tier 1 supplier to major engine manufacturers, the shop supports PPAP requirements and has maintained relationships with several Fortune 500 customers for more than 50 years.

The business emphasizes integrity, fair dealing, and continuous improvement to reduce cost while preserving quality. Its quality program targets zero defects, backed by CMM, optical comparator, surface-finish, Magnaflux, and Rockwell hardness inspection, and has earned a Dun & Bradstreet AAA rating.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automatic screw machining (up to 3.5\")", "CNC turning", "CNC multi-spindle chucking (up to 12\" diameter)", "Precision grinding (ID, OD, centerless, double disk, Blanchard)", "Broaching (internal/external, 54\" stroke, 15 ton)", "Thread rolling", "Knurling", "Drilling and tapping", "Cross drilling and deep hole drilling", "Countersinking", "Honing", "Milling", "Tumbling", "Bead blasting", "Cut to length", "Grooving, slotting, trimming, chamfering", "Precision assembly (brazing, mechanical fits)", "Heat treating (via qualified network)", "Coating (via qualified network)", "Ultrasonic cleaning", "Millipore testing / particle counting", "CMM inspection", "Profile measurement", "Optical comparator inspection"], "industries": ["Railroad", "Oil and gas", "Mining", "Emergency power generation", "Agricultural equipment", "Construction equipment", "Mine safety devices", "Heavy truck transmission", "Brake systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["25 automatic screw machines (capacity through 3.5\")", "CNC lathes", "CNC multi-spindle chuckers (up to 12\" diameter)", "12 broaching machines (54\" stroke, 15 ton)", "Grinding equipment (ID, OD, centerless, double disk, Blanchard)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "Close tolerance work; very close finish tolerances", "built_on": ["Founded in 1929 with nearly a century of continuous operation", "68,000 sq ft facility with 25 automatic screw machines and 12 broaching machines", "In-house precision assembly via brazing and mechanical fits", "Tier 1 supplier quality program with PPAP and Millipore particle-count testing", "Family-owned with Fortune 500 customer re