UPDATE companies SET description='Port Plastics was founded in 1960 in Albuquerque, New Mexico, as a regional supplier of industrial plastic materials to local manufacturers. Over six decades, the company expanded from a single location to a national network of 11 facilities positioned near major manufacturing hubs, including Houston for energy, San Jose for semiconductor, and Phoenix for aerospace and defense.

The company distributes high-performance engineering plastics — stocking more than 1,000 material grades such as PEEK, PTFE, Vespel, Torlon, and Ultem — and operates in-house fabrication shops equipped with precision CNC machining centers, CNC routers, and panel saws capable of cutting 5-inch-thick sheet up to 11 feet long. Services include routing, drilling, thermoforming, welding, and high-tolerance machining to ±0.001 inch, with same-day cutting and next-day delivery from local inventory.

Port Plastics serves semiconductor manufacturers requiring FM4910-compliant ultra-high-purity materials for wet benches and vacuum chambers; energy and oil-and-gas clients specifying NORSOK M-710-qualified components for subsea wellheads and sour-gas environments; aerospace and defense contractors needing AS9100D-compliant, FAR 25.853-compliant materials for structural panels, seals, and insulation; medical device makers using USP Class VI and ISO 10993 biocompatible polymers; and food processors relying on FDA 21 CFR 177 and NSF-certified materials for conveyor components and tank liners.

The company positions itself as a technical partner rather than a pure material supplier, emphasizing its staff of materials engineers averaging 15-plus years of plastics experience, full traceability documentation on every shipment, and a quality system certified to ISO 9001:2015 with additional AS9100D and ITAR registrations. Deep inventory positions and multiple source relationships are maintained to buffer customers against supply disruptions.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ITAR','FM4910','NORSOK M-710','FAR 25.853','FDA 21 CFR 177','NSF','USP Class VI','ISO 10993']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication", "Precision CNC machining", "CNC routing", "CNC panel saw cutting (5\" thick, 11'' long)", "Drilling", "Thermoforming", "Welding", "Precision cutting", "Panel saw cutting", "Fabrication and finishing", "High-tolerance machining (\u00b10.001 in)", "Material distribution", "Technical consulting and material selection", "Quality assurance and traceability", "Same-day delivery", "Inventory management"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Energy & Oil Gas", "Aerospace & Defense", "Medical & Life Sciences", "Food & Beverage Processing", "Marine", "Renewable Energy"], "materials": ["PEEK", "PTFE", "Polycarbonate", "Acrylic", "Vespel polyimide", "Torlon PAI", "Ultem PEI", "PVDF", "PPS", "UHMW", "Acetal", "HDPE", "PPSU (Radel)", "Polysulfone", "FDA-grade UHMW", "White FDA-grade acetal", "FDA HDPE", "Clear polycarbonate", "USP Class VI compliant polymers"], "equipment": ["Precision CNC machining centers", "CNC routers", "CNC Panel Saws (5\" thick, 11'' long)"], "volume": "Prototype to production runs", "lead_time": "Same-day cutting and next-day delivery for stocked materials", "tolerances": "\u00b10.001 in", "built_on": ["Same-day cutting and next-day delivery from 11 strategically located U.S. facilities", "Technical specialists averaging 15+ years of plastics industry experience", "Full traceability documentation and material certific