UPDATE companies SET description='Portland Bottling Company, founded in 1924, operates from Clackamas, Oregon, in the Portland metropolitan area. For nearly a century it has served as a fixture of the Pacific Northwest beverage industry, running multiple production, storage, and repacking facilities totaling roughly 500,000 square feet.

The company specializes in contract packing of ready-to-drink beverages in aluminum cans. Its capabilities cover filling, cartoning, secondary packaging, and warehousing. The canning line runs at up to 1,450 cans per minute and handles can sizes from 8.4 oz to 16 oz, with options for cold fill, tunnel pasteurization, liquid nitrogen dosing, reverse‑osmosis water treatment, and both liquid and granulated sweeteners. Cartoning equipment produces 4‑, 6‑, 8‑, 10‑, 12‑, and 24‑pack configurations, plus variety packs and registered film shrink wrap. On‑site and off‑site warehousing with 24/7 security supports distribution.

Portland Bottling works with and independent beverage brands across the Pacific Northwest and nationwide, shipping throughout the western United States and Canada. Its customer base includes producers of carbonated juices and waters, energy drinks, functional beverages, organic‑certified drinks, kosher beverages, and gluten‑free products.

The company emphasizes proactive partnership, treating customers’ resources as its own and maintaining rigorous quality systems. It holds FSSC 22000 certification, adheres to HACCP, and carries organic (QAI), gluten‑free (GFCO), and kosher (OU) certifications. Inline monitoring, on‑site QA labs, and third‑party audits underpin its quality assurance, while a “people‑first” culture aims to enable solutions at every production stage.', certifications=ARRAY['FSSC 22000','HACCP','Organic certification (Quality Assurance International)','Gluten-Free certification (Gluten Free Certification Organization)','Kosher certification (Orthodox Union)','Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum can filling (cold fill, tunnel pasteurization)", "Can sizing: 8.4 oz, 12 oz sleek, 12 oz standard, 16 oz standard", "Liquid nitrogen dosing", "Reverse osmosis water treatment", "Liquid and granulated sweetener handling", "Dilution ratios 1:3 to 1:5", "Cartoning: 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 24 packs and variety packs", "Registered film shrink wrapping", "Secondary packaging and multi-packing", "Repacking services", "On-site and off-site warehousing with 24/7 security", "On-site QA laboratories", "Inline automated quality monitoring", "Third-party audited quality systems", "Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) compliance"], "industries": ["Beverage co-packing", "Ready-to-drink (RTD) beverages", "Carbonated beverages", "Energy drinks", "Functional beverages", "Organic beverages", "Kosher beverages", "Gluten-free beverages"], "materials": ["Aluminum cans", "Beverage concentrates and bases", "Liquid sweeteners", "Granulated sweeteners", "Reverse osmosis water", "Liquid nitrogen"], "equipment": ["State-of-the-art canning line (up to 1,450 cpm)", "Automated cartoning and palletizing system", "Inline quality monitoring system", "Reverse osmosis water treatment system", "Liquid nitrogen dosing equipment"], "volume": "Up to 1,450 cans per minute", "lead_time": "", "toleran