UPDATE companies SET description='Portland Garment Factory (PGF) operates in Portland, Oregon. Founded in 2008 by Britt Howard, the studio is a woman-owned business certified by WBENC and a Certified B Corporation. It began as a zero-waste creative design and fabrication studio aiming to upend the traditional factory model through ethical labor practices and environmental sustainability.

PGF provides full-service creative design and fabrication, specializing in custom cut-and-sew manufacturing, art fabrication, product development, prototyping, and retail and experiential fabrication. The studio handles projects ranging from one-off installations to clothing production runs of 20,000-plus units. A team of 11 to 50 employees works in-house on fabrication, design, and experimentation through the PGF Lab, an internal incubator for unconventional projects.

Clients include major brands such as Nike, Adidas, Intel, Xbox, Converse, Tillamook, and agencies like Wieden+Kennedy, as well as artists and institutions including the Portland Art Museum and Portland Japanese Garden. Industries served span apparel manufacturing, retail display and installation, experiential marketing, public art and sculpture, corporate branding and merchandise, museum and cultural exhibits, sports and entertainment, and food and beverage packaging.

The company differentiates itself through a zero-waste philosophy, ethical labor practices, and a commitment to environmental sustainability. Its stated mission is to create work with intention and serve the community, guided by core values of being human, thinking forward, honoring process, respecting time, and inviting challenge.', certifications=ARRAY['Certified B Corporation','Certified Woman Owned Business (WBENC)','Sustainability at Work Gold Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cut-and-sew manufacturing", "Art fabrication", "Product development and prototyping", "Retail and experiential fabrication", "Design and ideation", "Installation and soft-goods fabrication", "Experimental materials research (PGF Lab)", "Pattern making and grading", "Sample development", "Small-batch and large-volume production"], "industries": ["Apparel manufacturing", "Retail display and installation", "Experiential marketing and events", "Public art and sculpture", "Corporate branding and merchandise", "Museum and cultural institutions", "Sports and entertainment", "Food and beverage packaging", "Furniture and interior fabrication", "Costume and mascot production"], "materials": ["Fabric and textiles", "Leather", "Upcycled and recycled materials", "Recycled polyester (NetPlus)", "Soft goods and flexible materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to 20,000+ units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-waste studio philosophy", "Ethical labor practices and environmental sustainability", "In-house experimentation lab (PGF Lab)", "Full-service clothing manufacturing up to 20,000+ units", "Certified B Corporation and WBENC-certified woman-owned"], "facts_used": ["Location: Portland, Oregon -> db", "Founded: 2008 -> /about", "Founder: Britt Howard -> /about", "Ownership: Woman-owned, WBENC certified -> /about", "Certifications: B Corp, WBENC, Sustainability at Work Gold -> /about", "Employee range: 11-50 from award category -> /about", "Services: