UPDATE companies SET description='Power Electronics International, Inc. (PE) is based in East Dundee, Illinois, where it designs, engineers, and manufactures variable frequency drives, soft-starts, motor control products, and automation systems for crane and hoist applications. The company operates its own production facility in East Dundee and emphasizes that all products are made in the United States.

PE’s product line includes Micro-Speed® VFDs, Smooth-Move® reduced torque control units, Multi-Vector® closed-loop hoist drives, regeneration resistors, and a range of custom and standard control panels for travel, hoist, and multi-motion crane systems. The company also develops add-on technologies such as the PE-SAM™ sensorless anti-sway system, the PE360™ rotating hook control, PLC-based automation packages, and the Mobi-Power™ wireless power system.

The company serves the overhead crane and hoist industry, including bridge cranes, trolley systems, monorails, gantry cranes, tower cranes, and boom cranes.

PE differentiates itself through its Upgrade-Path™ philosophy, which ensures that programming methods for current drives remain compatible with future models, and through its UL and cUL approvals for control panels and automation systems. The company also highlights its patented sensorless anti-sway technology and heavy-duty wireless power solution as unique offerings for demanding industrial environments.', certifications=ARRAY['UL approved','cUL approved']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Variable frequency drive (VFD) manufacturing", "Soft-start manufacturing", "Motor control product manufacturing", "Control panel design and manufacturing (travel motion, hoist, multi-motion, custom)", "Automation system integration (PLC automation)", "Regeneration resistor manufacturing", "Anti-sway control system development (PE-SAM)", "Rotating hook control system (PE360)", "Wireless power system development (Mobi-Power)", "Crane and hoist motion control solutions"], "industries": ["Overhead crane and hoist", "Bridge cranes", "Trolley systems", "Monorails", "Gantry cranes", "Tower cranes", "Boom cranes", "Industrial material handling", "Industrial automation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Upgrade-Path\u2122 philosophy: all past and present programming methods are subsets of future drive models", "All products designed, engineered, and manufactured in-house at East Dundee, Illinois facility", "PE-SAM\u2122: patented sensorless anti-sway technology integrated into Ultra Series drives", "PE Mobi-Power\u2122: heavy-duty wireless power system for industrial material handling", "UL and cUL approved manufacturer of control panels and automation systems"], "facts_used": ["Company name: Power Electronics International, Inc. -> db", "Headquarters: East Dundee, Illinois -> db, /", "Products: Micro-Speed\u00ae VFDs, Smooth-Move\u00ae reduced torque control units, Multi-Vector\u00ae drives, control panels, automation systems, resistors, PE-SAM, PE360, PLC Automation, Mobi-Power -> /, db", "Manufacturing location: East Dundee, Illinois facility -> /", "Scale: over a quarter of a million crane/hoist motions utilizing PE equipment -> /", "Certifications: UL and cUL approved manufacturer of control panels and automation systems -> /", "Differentiators: Upgrade-Path\u2122 philosophy, PE-SAM\u2122 sensorless anti-sway, PE Mobi-Power\u2122 wireless power -> /", "Industries served: crane and hoist, bridge cranes, trolley systems, monorails, gantry cranes, tower cranes, boom cranes -> /", "All products made in USA -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are proud to design, engineer, and manufacture all our equipment in our facility in East Dundee, Illinois USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='power-electronics-international-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Power Engineering & Manufacturing, Ltd. (PEM) was founded in 1975 by Saul Herscovici and members of the Warren family in Waterloo, Iowa. The company began as a specialist in custom gearbox design and has since grown into a full-service manufacturer of heavy-duty gearboxes serving customers across the United States and in more than 48 countries.

PEM designs, machines, assembles, and tests custom gearboxes from its Waterloo facility, which houses 12 CNC lathes, five CNC mills, two Okuma MCR-A5CII double-column machining centers, six CNC hobbing machines, five gear grinders, and a range of grinding, shaping, keyseating, welding, and inspection equipment. The shop can handle parts up to 78.7 inches in diameter and 96 inches in length, and offers reverse engineering, rebuild, and reconditioning services for virtually any make of gearbox, including Falk, Demag, Flender, and dozens of other OEM brands. In-house capabilities include finite-element analysis, proprietary gear-design software, magnetic-particle and visual inspection, and two large-capacity CMMs.

The company''s gearboxes operate in demanding applications such as U.S. Navy AD-43 systems, helicopter test stands, and roll crushers, and it supports maintenance and upgrade programs for industrial OEMs across sectors including defense, aerospace, mining, and general heavy industry. PEM also provides expedited manufacturing, climate-controlled warehousing, and 24/7 exchange programs for critical spares.

PEM emphasizes exceeding AGMA standards and achieving high power density through its MEGAGEAR® technology, which can increase horsepower or torque by up to 35 percent over original designs. The firm cites ingenuity, relentless attention to detail, and remarkable customer service as its defining differentiators, backed by an ISO 9001:2015 quality system and welding procedures qualified to AWS and NAVSEA standards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AWS D1.1','AWS D1.5','AWS D1.6','AWS D1.2','NAVSEA S9074-AR-GIB-010/278 (MIL STD-278)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom gearbox design and manufacturing", "Reverse engineering", "Gearbox rebuild and reconditioning", "Product inspection (CMM, magnetic particle, visual)", "Expedited manufacturing service", "Storage and stocking agreements", "CNC turning", "CNC milling", "CNC hobbing", "Gear grinding", "OD grinding", "Centerless grinding", "Shaper cutting", "Keyseating", "Plasma/torch cutting", "Saw cutting", "Dynamic balancing", "Robotic welding", "MIG welding (AWS D1.1, D1.5, D1.6, NAVSEA)", "Stress relieving", "Radial drilling", "Finite Element Analysis (FEA)", "Proprietary gear design software"], "industries": ["Defense", "Aerospace", "Mining", "Industrial Manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Okuma MCR-A5CII Double Column Machining Centers", "CNC Lathes (12)", "CNC Milling Machines (5)", "CNC Hobbing Machines (6)", "Gear Grinding Machines (5)", "CNC OD Grinding Machine", "Centerless Grinding Machine", "CNC Shaper Cutters (2)", "Keyseaters (2)", "CNC Plasma/Torch Machine", "CNC Saw Machine", "CNC Dynamic Balancing Machine", "Robotic Welding Machine", "Semi-Automatic MIG Welders (3)", "Stress Relief Furnace", "Radial Drills (2)", "Coordinate Measuring Machines (CMMs) (2)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom gearbox designs that exceed AGMA standards", "Proprietary MEGAGEAR\u00ae technology boosting power/torque up to 35%", "Reverse engineering and rebuild of a